Milestone 4 persistence authority cleanup

Reason
Several edge paths implemented their own document/PID writes or discarded an index rebuild error. This duplicated persistence policy and hid failures outside the owning authority.

Changes
- Make session_store_document the single serializer/sanitizer/atomic writer for sessions; startup orphan cleanup delegates to it and propagates index rebuild failure.
- Route Forecast and SearXNG PID receipts through private_store::atomic_write.
- Preserve the public storage migration error contract behind one wrapper.
- Replace one user-facing English project-store sentence with a stable error code.
- Restore the responsibility and format comments lost when the OOXML run writer was split.

Verification observed
- cargo test storage_migration -- --test-threads=1: 3 passed.
- cargo test subagent_startup_cleanup -- --test-threads=1: 4 passed.
- cargo test services::forecast::sidecar_process -- --test-threads=1: 2 passed.
- cargo test services::searxng::process -- --test-threads=1: 4 passed.
- cargo test tool_document_write -- --test-threads=1: 8 passed.
- cargo test app_build::tests -- --test-threads=1: 1 passed.
- git diff --check: passed.

Decision
The migration wrapper intentionally maps every private-store failure back to the pre-existing generic initialization error; this changes the persistence mechanism without changing its public IPC contract.
